 "title": "The POPREBEL semantic social network data",
 "url": "https://zenodo.org/records/7477600",
 "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.7477600",
 "description": "<p>The <a href=\"https://populism-europe.com/poprebel/\">POPREBEL project</a> explores the phenomenon of populism in Europe. As part of it, a team of ethnographers generated and coded the corpus contained in this dataset. It consists of coded interviews, realized between spring 2021 and spring 2022, to Internet users in Czechia, Germany and Poland, who used social media to gather information about the COVID-19 pandemic. The dataset is pseudonymized. POPREBEL is supported by the European Union&#39;s Horizon 2020 programme, grant n. 822682.</p>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li><a href=\"https://zenodo.org/record/7494327\">Final ethnographic report.</a> Section 1.2 contains a detailed description of how and why data were collected.</li>\n\t<li><a href=\"https://wellbeing.edgeryders.eu\">Funnel website</a> of the project.</li>\n\t<li><a href=\"https://hal.archives-ouvertes.fr/hal-02478720/document\">About semantic social networks</a>.</li>\n\t<li><a href=\"https://edgeryders.eu/t/long-term-ssna-data-storage-documentation-manual/12786\">Data export and documentation process</a> (contains links to the code used to export the data)</li>\n</ul>",
